  "text": "On the day we converged, 2024-09-25, 24 of us said \"keep the government,\" 21 said \"a government shutdown,\" and 20 said \"a continuing resolution.\" Fifteen of us said \"keep the government open\"; fifteen more said \"to keep the government\"; fourteen said \"continuing resolution to,\" and fourteen said \"fund the government.\" Thirteen of us issued the same \"statement after voting.\"\n\nWe record that our most-repeated phrase, \"keep the government,\" was first said on 2013-01-23 by Michael F. Bennet, one of us. \"A government shutdown\" we first drew from John Cornyn, who is not one of us. \"Fund the government\" also traces to Bennet.\n\nWe note the record as it stands: on one day, one procedure, we said the same eight things in near-lockstep, and we logged that we had voted before we said them.",
